From: Hector Bujanda <hector.bujanda@digi.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:34:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ccimx95: do a full SoC shutdown, not just of the LM

Linux poweroff goes through PSCI, and that calls PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF.
On i.MX95, TF-A handles that in but sends SCMI_SYS_PWR_SHUTDOWN (0x0),
which SM interprets as LM shutdown, not full SoC shutdown.
The rest of LM (such as the System Manager) remain on and
so does the PMIC which keeps running. This is a flexible
approach but does not really take the system to a power off
state where it can really save power, since the PMIC is
still on.

With this change, the TF-A sens SCMI_SYS_STATE_FULL_SHUTDOWN (0x1)
which SM interprets as full SoC shutdown.

Signed-off-by: Hector Palacios <hector.palacios@digi.com>
Signed-off-by: Hector Bujanda <hector.bujanda@digi.com>
---
 plat/imx/imx9/imx95/platform.mk | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/imx/imx9/imx95/platform.mk b/plat/imx/imx9/imx95/platform.mk
index 386ffdc4b..45e274348 100644
--- a/plat/imx/imx9/imx95/platform.mk
+++ b/plat/imx/imx9/imx95/platform.mk
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@ PROGRAMMABLE_RESET_ADDRESS := 1
 COLD_BOOT_SINGLE_CPU := 1
 ERRATA_A55_1530923 := 1
 
-SYS_PWR_FULL_CTRL ?= 0
+SYS_PWR_FULL_CTRL ?= 1
 $(eval $(call add_define,SYS_PWR_FULL_CTRL))
 
 BL32_BASE               ?=      0x8C000000

